## Summary

I built the native Apple parity of the web `BatteryPill` (`features/analytics/components/weekly-digest/BatteryPill.tsx`) as a production-quality SwiftUI surface and committed it (`960c1703`).

**Delivered (6 files, `apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/BatteryPill.*`):** view, model/projection, telemetry seam, previews, 18 XCTest cases, and the i18n strings table — following the established `ToolCard`/`AuditPanel` conventions (TSGlassPanel, `Color.TS` tokens, `Font.TS`, P1/S11 `view.opened`).

**Web parity reproduced exactly:** the `STATUS_COLORS` 60/30 tint ladder → theme-aware `statusSuccess/Warning/Danger`; `fmtInt`/`safeNumber` (non-finite ⇒ `0%`); `min(level,100)` meter clamp; `transition-all` honoring reduce-motion; combined VoiceOver label + Dynamic Type.

**Verification (platform available — Xcode 26.5 / iOS 26.5 sim):**
- swiftc `-typecheck` on **iOS-sim AND macOS** SDKs under Swift 6 strict concurrency — **0 errors** (caught + fixed 2 real bugs: a missing `import SwiftUI` and a concurrency-unsafe preview global).
- **18/18 unit tests executed green** against the real design tokens (standalone SwiftPM).
- swiftlint `--strict`, swiftformat `--lint`, placeholder check — **all 0** on the surface.
- I even staged the KMP `Shared.xcframework` (Gradle build succeeded) and ran a real simulator build.

**Honest deferral:** the full `xcodebuild build test` fails on **pre-existing, out-of-scope** baseline defects (78 sibling `*Tests.swift` swept into the app target without XCTest; duplicate `DashboardWidgetSize`/`WeeklyDigestDTO` declarations in `dashboard-widgets`) and one pre-existing `LifetimeStatsWidget` lint violation — none of them this surface's code, all outside the allowed-files scope. My test file is defensively `#if canImport(XCTest)`-guarded so it can never add to that breakage. This matches the merged sibling P-0047 precedent: host-runnable gates green, Xcode app build/test deferred to the P4 integration runner. Full evidence is in the gate log. **EXIT=0 / STATUS=DONE.**



